WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:01.440
Instructor: So the first thing we'll talk about

00:01.440 --> 00:04.590
is the difference between public and private repositories

00:04.590 --> 00:07.230
on GitHub, pretty straightforward.

00:07.230 --> 00:08.850
There are two settings, right?

00:08.850 --> 00:10.530
One setting with two options.

00:10.530 --> 00:13.410
You can make the visibility of any GitHub repository

00:13.410 --> 00:16.200
public or private, assuming that you're the owner

00:16.200 --> 00:19.320
and you have permission to make it public or private.

00:19.320 --> 00:20.940
So when you create a new repository,

00:20.940 --> 00:23.160
it prompts you with that choice.

00:23.160 --> 00:25.440
Here I have two GitHub accounts.

00:25.440 --> 00:26.850
The one I've been using, Colt,

00:26.850 --> 00:30.810
and then I made a new one for my chicken, Stevie Chicks.

00:30.810 --> 00:32.280
So that's Stevie Chicks.

00:32.280 --> 00:34.080
I'm also trying to make it clear up top,

00:34.080 --> 00:36.300
this is Stevie's account, and this one's mine,

00:36.300 --> 00:38.340
because here, it's somewhat easy to tell,

00:38.340 --> 00:41.010
but once we get on an actual repository page,

00:41.010 --> 00:42.750
if we're looking at the same repo,

00:42.750 --> 00:44.550
it's really hard to tell who is who.

00:44.550 --> 00:46.080
You can look at this little photo up there,

00:46.080 --> 00:47.880
but that's kind of, that's it.

00:47.880 --> 00:51.150
So I've put the name up top, Stevie and Colt.

00:51.150 --> 00:54.600
Anyway, if I make a new repository, new repository,

00:54.600 --> 00:56.730
we've seen that it prompts you for a name,

00:56.730 --> 01:00.000
and then here, public or private.

01:00.000 --> 01:01.740
So there's an important difference.

01:01.740 --> 01:05.190
A public repository is accessible, it's discoverable,

01:05.190 --> 01:08.130
it's clonable by anyone on the internet.

01:08.130 --> 01:10.710
They can go find your repo by searching on GitHub.

01:10.710 --> 01:14.040
They can find it by looking at your profile.

01:14.040 --> 01:16.620
They can just have the link and view it, right?

01:16.620 --> 01:18.300
Anybody can access it.

01:18.300 --> 01:19.530
That still does not mean

01:19.530 --> 01:22.320
people can change the contents of the repository.

01:22.320 --> 01:24.570
They can't push to the repository.

01:24.570 --> 01:26.760
They have to have collaborator privileges

01:26.760 --> 01:28.680
or permissions to do that.

01:28.680 --> 01:30.210
And I'll show you how to set that up,

01:30.210 --> 01:31.890
but that's a separate topic.

01:31.890 --> 01:34.410
We're purely talking about visibility.

01:34.410 --> 01:36.510
So anybody can see a public repo,

01:36.510 --> 01:38.400
but when I make something private,

01:38.400 --> 01:42.510
it's only accessible to the owner, AKA me who created it,

01:42.510 --> 01:45.420
and then people who have been granted access.

01:45.420 --> 01:48.750
So they have explicitly been added as collaborators.

01:48.750 --> 01:52.020
They then have access to a private repo.

01:52.020 --> 01:53.910
Now, things work slightly differently

01:53.910 --> 01:55.680
if we're talking about an organization

01:55.680 --> 01:57.900
or enterprise-level GitHub account

01:57.900 --> 02:00.480
where a private repository can be visible

02:00.480 --> 02:02.850
to everyone within the organization.

02:02.850 --> 02:05.370
But we're working with personal, free accounts.

02:05.370 --> 02:08.040
So a private repo is only visible to me, the owner,

02:08.040 --> 02:11.220
and people I specifically grant access to.

02:11.220 --> 02:13.170
So let's try making,

02:13.170 --> 02:16.020
sure, let's go with their name that they suggest,

02:16.020 --> 02:19.710
bookish disco, and then I'll make it public to start.

02:19.710 --> 02:20.543
Okay.

02:20.543 --> 02:23.100
I'll just create, we're not gonna do anything in here.

02:23.100 --> 02:24.660
I'm just making this repo,

02:24.660 --> 02:26.610
so anybody can see this now.

02:26.610 --> 02:29.700
If they go to my profile, go to repositories,

02:29.700 --> 02:32.220
here it is, bookish disco.

02:32.220 --> 02:36.360
Okay, so if I copy this over, I'm in Safari,

02:36.360 --> 02:39.060
I'm in a different browser here on Stevie's account,

02:39.060 --> 02:42.480
and if I go to this URL to view Colt,

02:42.480 --> 02:44.070
that's kind of why it's confusing, right?

02:44.070 --> 02:46.230
I'm viewing somebody else's account.

02:46.230 --> 02:47.910
I see bookish disco,

02:47.910 --> 02:50.100
even though I'm logged in as somebody else.

02:50.100 --> 02:52.980
Now, I don't see the same display.

02:52.980 --> 02:56.340
Like here, if I go to bookish disco, I'm the owner.

02:56.340 --> 02:58.680
So I see this information about getting set up,

02:58.680 --> 03:00.840
but I also see settings.

03:00.840 --> 03:02.640
I don't see that here.

03:02.640 --> 03:04.470
I'm just a member of the public

03:04.470 --> 03:07.620
viewing the repository because it's public.

03:07.620 --> 03:08.490
All right?

03:08.490 --> 03:11.610
So speaking of settings, if you wanna toggle

03:11.610 --> 03:15.240
or change that privacy under settings for a repository,

03:15.240 --> 03:16.830
you have to be the owner,

03:16.830 --> 03:19.050
unless we're talking about an organization

03:19.050 --> 03:20.880
or enterprise-level account.

03:20.880 --> 03:22.530
In that case, you don't have to be the owner,

03:22.530 --> 03:24.750
but you have to be granted permission

03:24.750 --> 03:26.370
to change the visibility.

03:26.370 --> 03:28.290
Anyway, if I wanna change visibility,

03:28.290 --> 03:31.530
it's under options, which we're already on, on settings,

03:31.530 --> 03:33.870
and then you just scroll for a long,

03:33.870 --> 03:35.760
long ways down to the very bottom.

03:35.760 --> 03:37.980
We're looking for the danger zone.

03:37.980 --> 03:39.480
And then we have this right here,

03:39.480 --> 03:42.090
change repository visibility.

03:42.090 --> 03:46.080
So I'm going to change visibility just to demonstrate this,

03:46.080 --> 03:48.300
and I'm going to make it private,

03:48.300 --> 03:50.730
but it's gonna ask me to type in,

03:50.730 --> 03:52.980
well, first, it actually just shows me

03:52.980 --> 03:54.720
all the changes that will happen.

03:54.720 --> 03:57.270
Anybody who is watching the repository,

03:57.270 --> 04:01.620
anybody who has starred it, you can star repositories,

04:01.620 --> 04:02.970
like here's an example.

04:02.970 --> 04:05.100
A couple hundred people have starred this one.

04:05.100 --> 04:05.970
People are watching it.

04:05.970 --> 04:07.320
They get notifications.

04:07.320 --> 04:10.650
So if I make that private, that goes away.

04:10.650 --> 04:12.750
But then also, there's some other changes

04:12.750 --> 04:14.640
that go along with making something private.

04:14.640 --> 04:16.140
I'll lose wikis

04:16.140 --> 04:18.690
and different poll requests and other things.

04:18.690 --> 04:20.250
Basically, we're going private,

04:20.250 --> 04:22.890
so anything involving the public goes away,

04:22.890 --> 04:24.630
but we don't have anything in here anyway.

04:24.630 --> 04:26.010
So I'm gonna type that.

04:26.010 --> 04:28.680
It wants me to exactly type the name of the repo.

04:28.680 --> 04:33.480
So colt/bookish-disco.

04:33.480 --> 04:34.650
All right, I understand.

04:34.650 --> 04:36.120
Change visibility.

04:36.120 --> 04:37.470
Now it wants my password.

04:37.470 --> 04:40.710
Okay, so now it shows up as private, right here.

04:40.710 --> 04:42.120
I'm on my account as Colt.

04:42.120 --> 04:44.310
I'm the owner, so I can see that.

04:44.310 --> 04:47.160
But if I refresh this page where I'm logged in as Stevie,

04:48.060 --> 04:50.190
404, I don't have access at all.

04:50.190 --> 04:51.840
I can't see that repository.

04:51.840 --> 04:53.100
I don't know it exists anymore.

04:53.100 --> 04:54.570
It's gone private.

04:54.570 --> 04:57.210
So that's the distinction and that's how you change them.

04:57.210 --> 04:59.850
Generally, it's a pain if you have a public repo

04:59.850 --> 05:01.860
and you make it private.

05:01.860 --> 05:03.240
I don't recommend, you know,

05:03.240 --> 05:05.220
having some big established repository

05:05.220 --> 05:06.690
with a whole bunch of collaborators

05:06.690 --> 05:10.680
and then going private and suddenly it's just gone.

05:10.680 --> 05:12.750
But you can do that, okay?

05:12.750 --> 05:14.070
Generally, I go the other direction.

05:14.070 --> 05:15.240
Start something in secret,

05:15.240 --> 05:17.790
start it private so people can't see them.

05:17.790 --> 05:21.600
For example, all these horrible little dumb demo repos

05:21.600 --> 05:23.670
that we have just for this course,

05:23.670 --> 05:25.770
all these Git repos like animals,

05:25.770 --> 05:28.440
colors, chickens, GitHub demo novel,

05:28.440 --> 05:30.270
I would normally make those private,

05:30.270 --> 05:32.700
and then maybe make them public.

05:32.700 --> 05:34.170
But I'm making them public

05:34.170 --> 05:35.580
because I want you to be able to see them.

05:35.580 --> 05:37.443
This is a Git course, okay.
